      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are 10 examples of subtle, non-slur-based racial microaggressions common in corporate settings. Examples include being repeatedly asked, \"Where are you *really* from?\" after stating a specific location, being mistaken for an assistant despite having a senior title, or having your unique cultural perspective dismissed by a teammate as \"just a cultural thing.\" Another subtle form is the assumption that your contributions are merely accommodations for your background rather than genuine expertise. Finally, \"diversity training\" being used as a catch-all excuse when substantive systemic changes are avoided.",
